        "text": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"shortdescription nomobile noexcerpt noprint searchaux\" style=\"display:none\">Instructions a computer can execute</div>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1368532237\">.mw-parser-output .hatnote{font-style:italic}.mw-parser-output div.hatnote{padding-left:1.6em;margin-bottom:0.5em}.mw-parser-output .hatnote i{font-style:normal}.mw-parser-output .hatnote+.mw-empty-elt+.hatnote{margin-top:-0.5em}@media print{body.ns-0 .mw-parser-output .hatnote{display:none!important}}</style><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\">For the TV program, see <a href=\"/wiki/The_Computer_Programme\" title=\"The Computer Programme\">The Computer Programme</a>.</div>\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\"><a href=\"/wiki/File:JavaScript_code.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/JavaScript_code.png/250px-JavaScript_code.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"250\" height=\"166\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/JavaScript_code.png/500px-JavaScript_code.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"882\" data-file-height=\"587\" /></a><figcaption><a href=\"/wiki/Source_code\" title=\"Source code\">Source code</a> for a computer program written in the <a href=\"/wiki/JavaScript\" title=\"JavaScript\">JavaScript</a> language. It demonstrates the <code>appendChild()</code> method. The method adds a new child node to an existing parent node. It is commonly used to dynamically modify the structure of an HTML document.</figcaption></figure>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1374427404\">.mw-parser-output .hlist dl,.mw-parser-output .hlist ol,.mw-parser-output .hlist ul{margin